### Check first
Check the timestamps of GenAI duration and token counters in the [caller’s metrics](/#/components/{{componentUrnForUrl}}/metrics). The threshold is **{{threshold}}** seconds. For an Open WebUI Ollama target with token samples alone, the gap is measured from the earliest token evidence in the observation window. The [caller](/#/components/{{componentUrnForUrl}}/highlights) shows the largest gap, capped at 900 seconds.

### Likely causes
The SDK or Collector stopped exporting duration samples. A metric filter or a change in cluster, instance, model or endpoint labels can also separate a duration counter from its token counter.

### Fix
Restore export of the duration histogram with the same caller and target labels. An idle client can continue exporting unchanged cumulative counts.

### Verify
Confirm that a fresh duration sample reaches each reporting target and the age falls below the threshold. If both duration and qualifying token counters are absent, the check can disappear after the observation window. Verify the exporter independently in that case.
